{"id":"ham","name":"Ham","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ham"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ham","text":"Warm, hot, and hence the south; also an Egyptian word meaning “black”, the youngest son of Noah (Gen. 5:32; comp. 9:22, 24). The curse pronounced by Noah against Ham, properly against Canaan his fourth son, was accomplished when the Jews subsequently exterminated the Canaanites. One of the most important facts recorded in Gen. 10 is the foundation of the earliest monarchy in Babylonia by Nimrod the grandson of Ham (6, 8, 10). The primitive Babylonian empire was thus Hamitic, and of a cognate race with the primitive inhabitants of Arabia and of Ethiopia. (See ACCAD.) The race of Ham were the most energetic of all the descendants of Noah in the early times of the post-diluvian world."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2526","lemma":"חָם","xlit":"Châm","gloss":"Cham, a son of Noah","kjv":"Ham","count":12,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H3667","lemma":"כְּנַעַן","xlit":"Kᵉnaʻan","gloss":"Kenaan, a son a Ham","kjv":"Canaan, merchant, traffick","count":9,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H8035","lemma":"שֵׁם","xlit":"Shêm","gloss":"Shem, a son of Noah","kjv":"Sem, Shem","count":6,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3568","lemma":"כּוּשׁ","xlit":"Kûwsh","gloss":"Cush , the name of a son of Ham, and of his territory","kjv":"Chush, Cush, Ethiopia","count":6,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H5146","lemma":"נֹחַ","xlit":"Nôach","gloss":"Noach, the patriarch of the flood","kjv":"Noah","count":6,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3315","lemma":"יֶפֶת","xlit":"Yepheth","gloss":"Jepheth, a son of Noah","kjv":"Japheth","count":5,"share":0.12}],"verses":["Gen.5.32","Gen.9.18","Gen.9.22","Gen.10.6","Gen.10.20","1Chr.1.4","1Chr.1.8","1Chr.4.40","Ps.78.51","Ps.105.23","Ps.105.27","Ps.106.22","Gen.9.19","Gen.9.20","Gen.9.21","Gen.9.23","Gen.9.24","Gen.9.25","Gen.9.26","Gen.9.27","Gen.10.7","Gen.10.8","Gen.10.9","Gen.10.10","Gen.10.11","Gen.10.12","Gen.10.13","Gen.10.14","Gen.10.15","Gen.10